  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1157 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nShowers and a few thunderstorms will linger this morning, before\nwe see some resurgence this afternoon. Higher chances are\nsimilar locations as Wednesday. There is a 30-70% chance for \ngusts over 35 mph, potentially peaking at 45-50 mph. The deeper \npush of monsoon moisture is moving away, but some decent \ndownpours are possible again through this evening. One last gasp\nfor thunderstorms is expected Friday with isolated storms \nacross the central mountains, eastern and southeastern \nhighlands, and across the Snake Plain. Storms will be dry, \nalthough the chance for outflow gusts over 35 mph is down to \n10-40%. Temperatures should be warmer both days, with some spots\npushing 100 Friday afternoon. \n\nA prolonged stretch of dry weather begins this weekend, as high\npressure is strongest on Saturday, then giving way next week to\na dry and breezy westerly flow. We will likely see some low to\nmid 100s Saturday. HeatRisk impacts will peak Saturday, and we\nmay need at least a HEAT ADVISORY for Saturday...if not both\nFriday and Saturday. With the ridge breaking down and\ntransitioning to westerly flow, winds will likely be strongest\nSaturday and Sunday. We MAY be approaching thresholds for Lake\nWind conditions on American Falls Reservoir and a Wind Advisory\nacross portions of the Snake Plain. Initially highs will drop\nback into the 80s and low 90s early next week, which is actually\nAVERAGE for the first week of August. It does appear though we\npush back into the low/mid 90s by midweek.",
